course: dictionary
lesson: 13408
title: Hewn: cut into shape by hand
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something was made. Hewn is one of them. The clue is in the sentence: «The steps were hewn from solid rock.» Rock is hard, so someone must have cut the steps out with sharp tools, not built them from bricks.
explain: Hewn is the past form of hew, which means to chop or cut with an axe, pick or other sharp tool. «The woodcutter hews the logs» means he is cutting now. «The logs were hewn by hand» means the cutting is finished.
explain: Hewn can also be an adjective, as in «a rough-hewn table». Rough-hewn means shaped roughly by cutting, so the surface is not smooth or polished. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «a table cut roughly into shape» still makes sense.
fact: Hew means to cut or chop with a sharp tool.
fact: «Hewn» is the past form of «hew», often used with was or were: «the stone was hewn».
fact: «Hewn» often describes wood or stone: «hand-hewn beams».
fact: «Rough-hewn» means shaped roughly by cutting, not smoothed.
fact: Old stone homes may be hewn from the rock, so their walls and rooms were cut out of the rock itself.
exercise: «The steps were hewn from solid rock.» What does hewn mean here? | *Cut into shape with a sharp tool | Melted by the sun | Built up from bricks | Painted bright blue
exercise: What does hew mean? | To hide something | To sing loudly | *To chop or cut with an axe or other sharp tool | To wash clothes
exercise: «The table was rough-hewn.» What does rough-hewn suggest? | Polished until it shone | Made of glass | Very light and thin | *Shaped roughly by cutting, not smoothed
test: «The beams in the old barn were hand-hewn.» What does hand-hewn tell you? | *Cut into shape by hand with tools | Painted by hand | Made by a machine in a factory | Found on a beach
test: Which word could replace hewn in «The statue was hewn from marble»? | Juggled | Sprinkled | Forgotten | *Carved
exam: Which sentence uses hewn correctly? | The song was hewn loudly. | The bread was hewn in the oven. | The sky was hewn at dawn. | *The old door was hewn from a single oak tree.
